    board(pm): file CF-181 — requirement ids and board task ids share the CF-nnn namespace
    
    Measured at 93ef524 from a fresh clone of origin/main. docs/PRD-code-factory.md opens a
    requirements table whose ID column runs CF-101, CF-102, ... (12 rows), and those ids are a
    REQUIREMENT namespace: the board carries no row for them. The milestone section then reuses the
    identical spelling for board rows and cites "CF-110 (no destroy path ships)" and "CF-112 (no
    dispatch-targets.jsonl consumer ships)" among "the open defects this milestone's legs depend on",
    closing with "The milestone cannot be claimed while any row above is open."
    
    Neither id has ever existed as a row: the probe prints cf110_row 0, cf112_row 0, cf110_events 0,
    cited_in_milestone 4, req_ids_in_prd 12; `grep -c 'CF-110' tasks.jsonl` = 2 matches, both inside
    other rows' prose; and `git log --all --oneline -S'"id":"CF-110"' -- tasks.jsonl` is empty, so no
    ref has ever carried such a row. The milestone's own membership rule is therefore not decidable
    for those two entries, which is the ambiguity this lane exists to remove.
    
    Filed P3, complexity 2, probe 553 chars, acceptance_criteria 1729 chars, reasoning 1847 chars.
    Filing only: no doc, script or test is changed by this commit; the repair is the pending row.
    
